ustain\\",\\"timeframe\\":\\"past-7-days\\",\\"unit\\":\\"points\\"}","[\\"Your {{value}} (0–4) on adjusting demands to available energy is at the lowest possible response value. Check whether that fits your experience and note exceptions the aggregate cannot show.\\",\\"Look for one sign of overload and a sustainable pace you can repeat without exhaustion.\\"]","[{\\"code\\":\\"answer-0\\",\\"displayRange\\":\\"0–<0.5\\",\\"from\\":0,\\"label\\":\\"Not at all\\",\\"levelLabel\\":\\"Rarely reported\\",\\"note\\":\\"In these answers, “A Pace I Can Sustain” is seldom reported. That is not a defect or diagnosis; explore the theme without pressure.\\",\\"optionalPractice\\":\\"Look for one sign of overload and a sustainable pace you can repeat without exhaustion.\\",\\"to\\":0.5},{\\"code\\":\\"answer-1\\",\\"displayRange\\":\\"0.5–<1.5\\",\\"from\\":0.5,\\"label\\":\\"A little\\",\\"levelLabel\\":\\"Occasionally reported\\",\\"note\\":\\"In these answers, “A Pace I Can Sustain” is reported occasionally. Notice safe situations in which it becomes available.\\",\\"optionalPractice\\":\\"Look for one sign of overload and a sustainable pace you can repeat without exhaustion.\\",\\"to\\":1.5},{\\"code\\":\\"answer-2\\",\\"displayRange\\":\\"1.5–<2.5\\",\\"from\\":1.5,\\"label\\":\\"Somewhat\\",\\"levelLabel\\":\\"Depends on context\\",\\"note\\":\\"In these answers, “A Pace I Can Sustain” varies by context. Compare situations where it feels easier with those where it feels harder.\\",\\"optionalPractice\\":\\"Look for one sign of overload and a sustainable pace you can repeat without exhaustion.\\",\\"to\\":2.5},{\\"code\\":\\"answer-3\\",\\"displayRange\\":\\"2.5–<3.5\\",\\"from\\":2.5,\\"label\\":\\"Quite a lot\\",\\"levelLabel\\":\\"Often reported\\",\\"note\\":\\"In these answers, “A Pace I Can Sustain” is often reported. Conditions, fatigue and stress can still make it variable; consistency is not required.\\",\\"optionalPractice\\":\\"Look for one sign of overload and a sustainable pace you can repeat without exhaustion.\\",\\"to\\":3.5},{\\"code\\":\\"answer-4\\",\\"displayRange\\":\\"3.5–4\\",\\"from\\":3.5,\\"label\\":\\"Very much\\",\\"levelLabel\\":\\"Consistently reported\\",\\"note\\":\\"In these answers, “A Pace I Can Sustain” is consistently reported. This is not a spiritual rank or a promise about every situation; choice and boundaries still matter.\\",\\"optionalPractice\\":\\"Look for one sign of overload and a sustainable pace you can repeat without exhaustion.\\",\\"to\\":4}]","{\\"code\\":\\"answer-0\\",\\"displayRange\\":\\"0–<0.5\\",\\"from\\":0,\\"label\\":\\"Not at all\\",\\"levelLabel\\":\\"Rarely reported\\",\\"note\\":\\"In these answers, “A Pace I Can Sustain” is seldom reported. That is not a defect or diagnosis; explore the theme without pressure.\\",\\"optionalPractice\\":\\"Look for one sign of overload and a sustainable pace you can repeat without exhaustion.\\",\\"to\\":0.5}","\\"Adjusting demands to available energy: {{value}} (0–4). Higher scores reflect greater endorsement of the statements about adjusting demands to available energy. This describes reported experience, not personal worth; an aggregate can hide differences between responses. Mean of 6 responses. No verified clinical categories are assigned to this result here. This is an original Holistic House self-reflection questionnaire. Its score must not be treated as a validated clinical assessment or evidence that an intervention works.\\"","\\"Higher scores reflect greater endorsement of the statements about adjusting demands to available energy. This describes reported experience, not personal worth; an aggregate can hide differences between responses.\\"","[\\"Use {{value}} (0–4) on adjusting demands to available energy as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. Compare only the same version, questionnaire language and reference period.\\",\\"Look for one sign of overload and a sustainable pace y