Compare situations where it feels easier with those where it feels harder.\\",\\"optionalPractice\\":\\"If it feels safe, name one feeling to a trusted person, or write it privately instead.\\",\\"to\\":2.5},{\\"code\\":\\"answer-3\\",\\"displayRange\\":\\"2.5–<3.5\\",\\"from\\":2.5,\\"label\\":\\"Quite a lot\\",\\"levelLabel\\":\\"Often reported\\",\\"note\\":\\"In these answers, “Emotional openness” is often reported. Conditions, fatigue and stress can still make it variable; consistency is not required.\\",\\"optionalPractice\\":\\"If it feels safe, name one feeling to a trusted person, or write it privately instead.\\",\\"to\\":3.5},{\\"code\\":\\"answer-4\\",\\"displayRange\\":\\"3.5–4\\",\\"from\\":3.5,\\"label\\":\\"Very much\\",\\"levelLabel\\":\\"Consistently reported\\",\\"note\\":\\"In these answers, “Emotional openness” is consistently reported. This is not a spiritual rank or a promise about every situation; choice and boundaries still matter.\\",\\"optionalPractice\\":\\"If it feels safe, name one feeling to a trusted person, or write it privately instead.\\",\\"to\\":4}]","{\\"code\\":\\"answer-0\\",\\"displayRange\\":\\"0–<0.5\\",\\"from\\":0,\\"label\\":\\"Not at all\\",\\"levelLabel\\":\\"Rarely reported\\",\\"note\\":\\"In these answers, “Emotional openness” is seldom reported. That is not a defect or diagnosis; explore the theme without pressure.\\",\\"optionalPractice\\":\\"If it feels safe, name one feeling to a trusted person, or write it privately instead.\\",\\"to\\":0.5}","\\"Emotional openness: {{value}} (0–4). Higher scores reflect greater endorsement of the statements about emotional openness. This describes reported experience, not personal worth; an aggregate can hide differences between responses. Mean of 3 responses. No verified clinical categories are assigned to this result here. This is an original Holistic House self-reflection questionnaire. Its score must not be treated as a validated clinical assessment or evidence that an intervention works.\\"","\\"Higher scores reflect greater endorsement of the statements about emotional openness. This describes reported experience, not personal worth; an aggregate can hide differences between responses.\\"","[\\"Use {{value}} (0–4) on emotional openness as a starting observation: describe a concrete situation and its impact on the day. Compare only the same version, questionnaire language and reference period.\\",\\"If it feels safe, name one feeling to a trusted person, or write it privately instead.\\"]","{\\"code\\":\\"answer-1\\",\\"displayRange\\":\\"0.5–<1.5\\",\\"from\\":0.5,\\"label\\":\\"A little\\",\\"levelLabel\\":\\"Occasionally reported\\",\\"note\\":\\"In these answers, “Emotional openness” is reported occasionally. Notice safe situations in which it becomes available.\\",\\"optionalPractice\\":\\"If it feels safe, name one feeling to a trusted person, or write it privately instead.\\",\\"to\\":1.5}","{\\"code\\":\\"answer-2\\",\\"displayRange\\":\\"1.5–<2.5\\",\\"from\\":1.5,\\"label\\":\\"Somewhat\\",\\"levelLabel\\":\\"Depends on context\\",\\"note\\":\\"In these answers, “Emotional openness” varies by context. Compare situations where it feels easier with those where it feels harder.\\",\\"optionalPractice\\":\\"If it feels safe, name one feeling to a trusted person, or write it privately instead.\\",\\"to\\":2.5}","{\\"code\\":\\"answer-3\\",\\"displayRange\\":\\"2.5–<3.5\\",\\"from\\":2.5,\\"label\\":\\"Quite a lot\\",\\"levelLabel\\":\\"Often reported\\",\\"note\\":\\"In these answers, “Emotional openness” is often reported. Conditions, fatigue and stress can still make it variable; consistency is not required.\\",\\"optionalPractice\\":\\"If it feels safe, name one feeling to a trusted person, or write it privately instead.\\",\\"to\\":3.5}","{\\"code\\":\\"answer-4\\",\\"displayRange\\":\\"3.5–4\\",\\"from\\":3.5,\\"label\\":\\"Very much\\",\\"levelLabel\\":\\"Consistently reported\\",\\"note\\":\\"In these answers, “Emotional openness” is consistently reported. This is not a spiritual rank or a promise about every situation; choice and boundaries still matter.\\",\\"optionalPractice\\":\\"If it feels safe, name one feeling to a trusted person, or write it privately instead.\\",\\"to\\":4}","[\\"Your {{value}} (0–4) on emotional openness is at the highest possible response value. Note where this appears and where your experience differs; this is not a clinical threshold.\\",\\"If it feels safe, name one feeling to a trusted person, or write it privately instead.\\"]","{\\"dimensionClass\\":\\"resources\\",\\"direction\\":\\"higher-reported-resource\\",\\"key\\":\\"resources.emotional_intimacy.pacing\\",\\"max\\":4,\\"min\\":0,\\"sourceConstruct\\":\\"Choosing the pace\\",\\"timeframe\\":\\"past-30-days\\",\\"unit\\":\\"points\\"}","[\\"Your {{value}} (0–4) on choosing the pace is at the lowest possible response value. Check whether that fits your experience and note exceptions the aggregate cannot show.\\",\\"Before an important exchange, check whether you want contact, privacy, or more time; you may change your mind.\\"]","[{\\"code\\":\\"answer-0\\",\\"displayRange\\":\\"0–<0.5\\",\\"from\\":0,\\"label\\":\\"Not at all\\",\\"levelLabel\\":\\"Rarely reported\\",\\"note\\":\\"In these answers, “Choosing the pace” is seldom reported. That is not a defect or diagnosis; explore the theme without pressure.\\",\\"optionalPractice\\":\\"Before an important exchange, check whether you want contact, privacy, or more time; you may change your mind.\\",\\"to\\":0.5},{\\"code\\":\\"answer-1\\",\\"displayRange\\":\\"0.5–<1.5\\",\\"from\\":0.5,\\"label\\":\\"A little\\",\\"levelLabel\\":\\"Occasionally reported\\",\\"note\\":\\"In these answers, “Choosing the pace” is reported occasionally. Notice safe situations in which it becomes available.\\",\\"optionalPractice\\":\\"Before an important exchange, check whether you want contact, privacy, or more time; you may change your mind.\\",\\"to\\":1.5},{\